<title>SWITZERLAND: POLL - Swiss interest rates seen heading higher.</title>
<headline>POLL - Swiss interest rates seen heading higher.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss interest rates are expected to move higher, according to a monthly poll of leading Swiss banks by the Finanz und Wirtschaft newspaper:</p>
<p>		    Three-month Eurofrancs   10-year govt bond yield</p>
<p> (in pct)	in 3 months   in 12 mos   in 3 months  in 12 mos</p>
<p> Credit Suisse 1.4 (1.4)   1.6  (2.0)   3.5 (3.5)    3.6  (4.0)</p>
<p> UBS	     1.5 (1.5)   2.0  (2.0)   3.4 (3.5)    3.8  (3.8)</p>
<p> SBC Warburg   1.4 (1.5)   2.25 (2.25)  3.5 (3.75)   4.0  (4.0)</p>
<p> Julius Baer   1.0 (1.0)   1.75 (1.7)   3.3 (3.4)    3.6  (3.7)</p>
<p> ZKB	     1.5 (1.5)   1.8  (1.8)   3.6 (3.6)    3.8  (3.8)</p>
<p> Average	 1.36(1.38)  1.88 (1.95)  3.46 (3.55)  3.76 (3.86)</p>
<p>(June forecast in brackets)</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
